+# Full odd-star infrared cold review
+
+**PASS under the explicit8062/8063 hypotheses**, for DERIVATION58b7617ddd948491a69493c8aee09174d72ab2c85060dc04d844d6a2b022694c. Complete proof read independently. Reuses previously reviewed uniform odd quasi-local creators, pure Gaussian AP references, thermodynamic local convergence and wrong-flux construction; no physical calculation or positivity assumption. This reviewer authored the Gaussian-extraction and thermodynamic predecessor reviews.
+
+1. For a normalized Bloch annihilator, its Majorana coefficients are bounded by a cell-dependent constant/sqrt(Ncell), independent of an eigenvector gauge. Graded locality restricts its anticommutator with a local odd D to D's support. Since annihilators kill the vacuum, the resulting norm estimate controls ALL particle sectors. On every occupation vector, positive total energy<=epsilon implies an occupied mode of frequency<=epsilon; thus the low-total-energy projection is bounded by the low-mode number operator. It is not being replaced by a one-particle projector. The same diagonal reasoning proves the inverse-power occupation inequality.
+
+2. The AP minimum-frequency bound absorbs the +1 in finite-grid ball counting; finite bands/nodes and cell volume only change constants. Exact-zero grids would fail this step and are excluded. Dyadic odd shells have support O(r³) and arbitrarily rapid norm decay, so sum m||D|| converges. Triangle inequality is used on projected VECTOR norms before squaring, giving the asserted cubic spectral tail with a uniform constant. The final whole-torus tail is harmless because its support is O(L³) and its norm can use p>3.
+
+3. Stieltjes integration gives C epsilon^(3-s)+s C epsilon^(3-s)/(3-s)=3C epsilon^(3-s)/(3-s). Hence q<3/2 for inverse-vector domains is correct; the endpoint is not proved. Oddness removes the vacuum atom. The estimates do not use a many-body active gap or separate independence among excited particles.
+
+4. The time-correlation identity uses the same dynamics sign as the predecessor. Fixed-ball/operator/state convergence establishes characteristic-function convergence; commutator bounds supply uniform positive-energy second moments if desired. Local polynomials are in the derivation domain and summable commutator shells extend that domain by closedness. Low-energy continuous cutoffs pass the cubic estimate to the limit and exclude a new zero atom, so weak convergence plus the uniform E^-s tail justifies the inverse moments. Polarization handles complex cross entries. No global identification of periodic Fock spaces is invoked.
+
+5. Subtracting the actual extracted linear creator is legitimate: a linear Majorana operator acting on the vacuum creates only one quasiparticle, and its coefficients have the parent's weighted-l1 convergence and rapid tails. Thus Z=Y-L is another uniformly quasi-local odd family with vacuum image exactly the higher-odd part. This avoids assuming convergence of number projectors themselves. It yields existence and nonnegativity of the limiting higher-sector susceptibility, not positivity from L6.
+
+6. The new graded Bessel step is essential and valid. Disjoint odd approximants anticommute, giving a summable norm bound g(v,w) on {Y_v*,Y_w}. For complex coefficients, A*A<=A*A+AA*, so ||A||²<=||{A*,A}||; Schur's estimate then bounds the translate map from l2 into Fock space. Composing its adjoint with H^-1 chi_v yields the full row-l2 bound. This is stronger than individual-vector inverse bounds alone, and does not imply bounded global convolution norm or row-l1. The infinite version follows from the same local estimate, not an unproved strong-row limit. Complex spectator coefficients need the stated sqrt2 factor, while real rows have exact CAR l2 norm.
+
+No blocker found. The conclusion is full odd singleton response control and its thermodynamic inverse moments in the supplied Gaussian reference. It does not identify the full physical sixth-order Hamiltonian, establish an interacting phase, determine a Dirac-node value, or solve fixed-U local defect stability. Constants remain existence bounds dependent on the inherited local/filter parameters. Planned tiny controls are not yet execution evidence in this review.
